 Each of the 18 rounds has seven phases:
 
-1. **Hour Glass:** Start Player reveals the top tile. Most events wait until Phase 6; Pilgrimage instead prohibits Monk recruitment during Phase 5.
+1. **Hour Glass (reveal):** Start Player reveals the top tile in Phase 1. Revealing announces the event; it does not resolve it. Normal events apply in Phase 6. **Pilgrimage is revealed in Phase 1 but applies in Phase 5 (Actions)**, when it prohibits Monk recruitment.
 2. **Census:** Compare markers on the Farmers Track, regardless of how many Farmer tiles are currently in bags. The unique leader gains 1 coin; a tied lead gives no coin. The unique last player pays 1 coin; a tied last place pays nothing. **In a 2-player game the last player never pays**, but a unique leader still gains 1 coin.
 3. **Followers:** Draw any number up to the allowance shown on your Knights Track (initially 4), limited by free Market spaces. Unused Market Followers remain between rounds and occupy capacity. You may inspect your bag at any time, but shuffle its contents afterward. For each draw you decline, you may instead move one Follower from an Action Space back to your Market. This is the permitted way to recover assigned Followers; you cannot move a Follower directly from one Action Space to another.
 4. **Planning:** Assign Market Followers to matching Action Spaces on your board and acquired Places. You may leave Followers on the Market or fill an action gradually over multiple rounds. An action is activated only when all required spaces are occupied by Followers or legal Technology. Town Hall is an exception: one of its two spaces is enough. An activation can be saved for a later round. Begin planning simultaneously; announce completion. If order matters, plan in clockwise order from Start Player.
-5. **Actions:** Starting with Start Player, go clockwise repeatedly, taking **one activated action or passing** per turn. Choose your actions' order freely. A Place completed during this Action Phase is available on a later one of your action turns in the same phase; it does not have to wait until the next round. You must not have passed. Passing ends your participation in this Action Phase, even if other players continue or you have unused activations. The phase ends when everyone has passed. After executing an ordinary action, return the Followers used for it to your bag; Technology stays on its spaces. Town Hall instead sends its selected Followers permanently to Beneficial Deeds. Unused activations, and incomplete actions, keep their Followers on the board for future rounds.
+5. **Actions:** If this round has Pilgrimage, apply its no-Monk-recruitment restriction **during this phase, Phase 5**. Starting with Start Player, go clockwise repeatedly, taking **one activated action or passing** per turn. Choose your actions' order freely. A Place completed during this Action Phase is available on a later one of your action turns in the same phase; it does not have to wait until the next round. You must not have passed. Passing ends your participation in this Action Phase, even if other players continue or you have unused activations. The phase ends when everyone has passed. After executing an ordinary action, return the Followers used for it to your bag; Technology stays on its spaces. Town Hall instead sends its selected Followers permanently to Beneficial Deeds. Unused activations, and incomplete actions, keep their Followers on the board for future rounds.
 6. **Event:** Resolve this round's event for all players (Pilgrimage already affected Actions). Payments, and any necessary order-sensitive resolution, proceed clockwise from Start Player. Coins paid go into the common supply; received coins come from it.
 7. **Start Player:** Pass the token to the player on your left.
 
